WEBVTT

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:40.070
Cut it out... Father...

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.880
- Lady Fena!
- Lady Fena!

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.700
You're finally awake?
Thank goodness!

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.880
You had us a little worried!

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.670
You've been asleep
for nearly half a day!

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:04.770
You can rest easy!
We've managed to escape the island!

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.520
Salman... Otto...

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.410
We escaped from the island?

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.650
The tide and the wind
were both on our side!

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:29.290
You're safe now!

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.790
- Lady Fena?
- Sorry!

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.300
I must apologize. With you unconscious, we were
unable to ask what you wanted us to do.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.540
What're you saying?
This is fine! This is perfect!

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.810
- Er, but you seemed--
- I was out of it after waking up, that's all.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.810
Lady Fena...

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:58.070
I'm glad I put my trust in you two.
Thank you, Otto! Salman!

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.560
L-Lady Fena!

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.640
Your words are far too kind!

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.940
If it was for you, Lady Fena,

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.960
- I would gladly walk through fire!
- Come on, don't be like that...

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.460
That reminds me,
what is Brule doing here?

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.820
That dog refused to
leave your side, Lady Fena.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.840
- Is that a problem?
- Hardly!

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.840
Brule!

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.090
Come to think of it,
how did you get that?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.600
Oh. I got this from the helmeted
swordsman who saved me.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:30.980
Helmeted swordsman?

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.110
The pair that saved me
were wearing helmets, too.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.320
That swordsman bonked me
on the head!

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.110
Who is he?
You know, don't you Otto?

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.530
Otto!

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.570
Otto?

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.390
Where in the world
did that island come from?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.230
Goblin Island.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.320
Our guests are here!

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.890
Well, well. They really
made it here.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:25.320
Those old-timers
actually pulled it off.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.950
Our mission is complete.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.540
Are you sure that
coming in here a good idea?

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:45.760
This is the only way in.
Salman, put us in over there.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.230
This is amazing...

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.510
Otto, what is this place?

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.020
- An old comrade-in-arms lives here.
- Who's that?

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.530
He saved my life
during the Spanish War.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:10.870
He was a fearsome
swordsman indeed.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.410
I remember his eyes as clearly
as if it were yesterday.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.520
You smell <i>igusa,</i> rush grass.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.940
I suppose Westerners
are not familiar with its aroma.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.940
Priest, we have brought her
as promised.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.180
You never said anything about
sending help!

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:49.120
Don't get so worked up
over it, Otto.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.200
If their presence proved helpful,
that is what matters.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.710
Beyond any doubt,
this is Fena Houtman.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.460
You are as lovely
as the stories say.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:05.580
My name is Yukihisa Sanada.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:08.300
I serve as master of this island.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.600
Er, I'm Fena Houtman.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.920
- To my right is my colleague--
- I am Salman, a Houtman knight.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.340
Ah, Sir Salman.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.100
No, Sir Yukuhisa, my name
is not Salman, it is Salman.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.430
- Salman?
- No, Salman.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:25.060
- Salman?
- Sa-l-man!

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.820
His name is Salman!

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.240
More importantly, Master Yukihisa...

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.990
Please tell me the reason
I am here.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.550
Very well.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.930
I shall tell you about this place.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:58.100
Various circumstances found our great-grandfathers
wandering the seas of the world.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.400
They lost their rudder in a storm,
and their ship grounded itself on the beach.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:07.720
The ones who saved them, shivering from cold
and hunger in an unfamiliar land,

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:12.570
and bequeathed them this place
was its lord, the Houtman family.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.240
Ever since, we have protected his descendants,
both openly and in secret,

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:20.250
in the hopes of repaying
that debt.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:25.380
Franz was a good friend, at whose side
I fought in many a battle.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.630
My father?

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.130
Do you remember Yukimaru?

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.520
I... I remember him.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.690
That night, your father
entrusted this to Yukimaru.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.280
Father did that?

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.280
"Protect it with your very life."

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.280
Those were Franz's last words.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:00.860
I suspect that what we are meant to protect
is located where this stone came from.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:02.750
But I know not
what that might be.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:07.070
Many years passed with us
unable to answer that question,

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:09.300
and just as we were
at our wits' end,

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:13.800
I received word from Otto
that you were still alive.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:27.020
Lady Fena, is there anything
that you can tell us about this?

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.780
I've... never seen it before.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:37.780
You father ought to have told you
about it in some way or another.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.950
He told <i>me</i> about it?

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:43.040
Honest, I really
don't know anything.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:48.040
We wish to carry out your father's
dying words no matter the cost.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:52.590
And as for the mystery
of this stone he left with us...

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:55.430
Lady Fena Houtman,

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:59.260
only you know the answer.

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:09.270
I'm the only one
with the answers...

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.490
I don't know anything either!

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.400
Did you sleep well?

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:42.470
Over here. Hi.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.470
Who are you?

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.080
The name's Karin.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:49.230
The priest told me
to show you around.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:54.150
This is called an automatic hammer.
It's powered by springs.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:57.150
You see, this was--
Are you even listening to me?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.620
- Yes, of course! Of course!
- Sure you were.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.160
Fine, whatever.
I'll start again from the top.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:08.040
This is an automatic hammer designed by
yours truly. It's powered by springs, and--

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:12.670
Hey, I know! Let's make a <i>tanto</i>
for you, and where did she go?!

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.940
Those bows are so pretty...

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.320
Are you interested in bows?

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:43.580
The color looks a bit different
out in the sun.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.570
It's huge! But light!
And pretty!

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:52.070
The dye is made from
sea snail shells.

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:54.450
- I love this color!
- Oh. Why, thank you.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:55.780
What's your name?

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.710
- My name is--
- Hey, Makaba!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:02.470
That bow is special.
Only he can make ones like it.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.470
And there's only one person
on the whole island who can use it.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:08.480
Only one person?

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:22.780
Amazing! Wonderful!
Every movement you make is beautiful!

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.500
Okay, she's all yours.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:32.920
Care to try?

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:36.040
- Can I really?
- Is it okay, Makaba?

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.050
Why won't they fly far?!

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.140
Aw, I don't get it!

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.310
- Darn it, I'll get it this time!
- Excuse me.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.240
Strength isn't the key.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.850
Now, just watch closely.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:07.450
- I just need to aim for the middle, right?
- That's right.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:12.120
- But the target will tempt you.
- It will?

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.130
Don't let it distract you.

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.380
The target...

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:29.590
I hit it! It kinda went like this
and then that and then this again!

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:30.500
Did you see?!

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.060
It went "whoosh" and curved!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:33.690
Whoosh?

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.190
Whoosh?

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.020
Whoosh!

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:44.950
You're Fena, yes?

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.690
I'm Shitan.
Welcome to the island.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.700
- If you have any questions--
- Hey!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.450
It's time for <i>kobiru!</i>

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.210
<i>Kobiru?</i>

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:58.660
Ah, <i>kobiru</i> is a light meal you eat
between breakfast and lunch.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:01.210
Oh, it's like a snack!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.220
Like this?

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:05.800
That's perfect.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.590
Now we baste them with miso
and grill them.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.600
- Tsubaki, can I help with--
- Don't set foot in here!

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:14.770
- Why not?
- He wouldn't know good food if it bit him.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.400
What a smell!

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.990
- They're gonna taste just as good, right?
- You better believe it.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.030
Oo, she's pretty!

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:29.650
Are you Fena?

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:32.370
- She's pretty, all right!
- I'm Enju!

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.750
- And I'm Kaede!
- Yeah! We're twins!

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.530
- Well?
- Well?

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:38.990
Who do you like better?

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:41.630
Sorry, I knew I was forgetting something!
Allow me to introduce these two, Fena.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:45.660
These are ants #1 and #2.
If they ever bother you, feel free to squash 'em.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:47.930
- Sure...
- They're ready!

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:51.890
What's with this shape?

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.960
Oh! That's shaped like a heart!
Isn't it cute?

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.420
Yep! It sure is!

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:59.770
- Hm? Where's Yukimaru?
- He said he wasn't hungry.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.900
- Hup!
- Can't you eat like normal people?!

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.150
Yukimaru...

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.700
That does it! Now I'm mad!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:15.410
Come back here! How many times do I
have to tell you not to waste food?!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.660
Hold still!

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.810
<i>Raicho,</i> "thunderbirds."

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:41.840
They don't migrate.
They've always been on this island.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:43.890
They're poor flyers, apparently.

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:45.730
Oh.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.830
It sure has been a long time, Yukimaru!

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:03.410
You sure got tall, huh? When we were kids,
you were always a little shorter than me.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:05.340
Everyone kept calling you
runt or pipsqueak--

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.340
Stop talking.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.220
You hit me again!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.110
- That stone--
- I wanted to--

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:27.930
You go.

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:32.850
I wanted... I wanted to thank you.
Ever since that night on the <i>Hope.</i>

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:33.980
That's not necessary.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:36.120
- You saved me, so--
- You're not saved.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.620
You haven't been saved.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:43.500
Have you solved
the riddle of the stone?

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.760
Oh, this? No, I still don't
remember anything.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.950
You're the only one
who can solve the riddle.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:50.510
That's what our priest said.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:55.050
- That's what he says, but still...
- Nothing about it rings any bells?

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:02.020
Why would Franz bring his beloved daughter
along on such a dangerous voyage?

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.510
I don't know what his
true intentions were.

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:09.280
But if the goal of the journey had something
to do with you, it makes more sense.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.150
With me?

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:14.780
- But I don't remember anything, honest.
- Grow up!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:19.540
Franz lost his life
on that voyage.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:25.360
Your father was willing to give his life
to see that voyage through.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:27.960
Aren't you curious to know
what it was meant for?

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.800
In our lives, we have duties
and responsibilities.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.760
That is the lot of all those who have
been given the gift of a heartbeat.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.890
Only a coward would
run from them.

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:40.060
I'm...

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:10.590
The meaning behind
father's voyage...

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.850
The lot of all those given
the gift of a heartbeat...

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.260
What happened to your hair?

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:02.850
I cut it off!

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:10.400
And has doing so
helped you remember?

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:16.070
You said that only I could solve
the riddle of the stone.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.280
I did.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:21.160
I started to believe it myself.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:25.320
So I decided to do something
to try to remember.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:28.660
About that day that I've wanted to forget
more than anything in the world.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.790
There's a hazy memory.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:37.170
Of a single word that my father said to me.
He said...

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:39.800
"Eden."

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:44.670
Where do you suppose my father
was trying to take me?

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:47.230
Why do you suppose
he was he killed?

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:50.600
What reason could he have had
to set out on such a dangerous voyage?

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:56.230
If solving the riddle of this stone might be
a clue to answering those questions,

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.070
then I want to know.

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:06.660
My father's voyage
ended before he could finish it.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.820
But I'm here.

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:12.830
I'll pick up my father's voyage
where he left off.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.470
Lady Fena.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:23.930
That stone is not of this island.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:27.350
I suspect it would not be possible to solve
its mystery if you were to stay here.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.060
I understand that.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:31.270
But I still--

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:46.330
Everyone here should be
familiar to you by now.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:53.210
They are the foremost fighting force
on the island, each a mighty warrior.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:57.340
In addition, I shall lend you
the use of a ship.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:59.460
You really mean it?!

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:05.640
It is our duty to keep you safe,

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.720
Fena Houtman.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.930
- Everyone, is this clear?
- Aye!

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:21.860
Wow!

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:25.740
- Karin, you built this?!
- I only designed it.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:28.980
It's my dad who actually built it.
He's a shipwright.

00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:31.820
It's powered by springs.
Hang on, not springs.

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:33.250
Cut that out, damn it!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.750
We can't keep you two safe, too!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:37.130
- Why can't we come?!
- You're letting the dog come!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:39.880
Men your age shouldn't be
bawling like babies!

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:49.460
Don't worry about me.
We'll see each other soon.

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:51.770
Just have faith in me
and watch over me.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:56.880
Lady Fena, take care
not to catch cold!

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:00.020
Be careful out there!

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:04.030
We'll be waiting for you!

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.160
Yukimaru.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.410
Here, this is yours.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:20.170
You forgot your sword yesterday.
I borrowed it for a bit.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:25.130
Keep it.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:29.350
I was honing swords
that Karin had forged.

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:30.680
You use it.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:32.310
Thank you.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:37.350
Your hair... You cut it.

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.230
It's nice.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.230
Hm? Did you say something?

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:47.320
Yukimaru, I didn't hear you.
Yukimaru! Yukimaru!

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.240
Yukimaru! C'mon, Yukimaru!

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:51.120
Yukimaru! Yukimaru!
Yukima--

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:54.910
- Why did you hit me?!
- You keep talking.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:54.940
- This ship's called the <i>Small Fry</i>, right?
- <i>Small Fry! Small Fry!</i>

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:58.040
Are you making fun
of my ship, ant?

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.040
You talk too softly!

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:59.710
And you talk too loudly!
Just like always!

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:01.130
Tsubaki, I'm starving!
Make me something!

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.130
SHUT UP!

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.130
Shut up!
